## §22. CI INTEGRITY GATES

### 22.1 Full CI integrity trigger list

CI MUST fail immediately if ANY of the following conditions are detected:

| # | Condition | Detection method |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Required phase artifact is missing | Check `docs/reports/plans/` for expected file per phase |
| 2 | Phase claims do not match artifact status | `FACT_CLASSIFICATION` section missing or has UNRESOLVED items |
| 3 | Broad pytest run before final phase | `pytest tests/` or `pytest tests/unit` in any phase < final |
| 4 | Unexpected skip or xfail appears | Skip/xfail not in pre-existing skip registry (§17) |
| 5 | Failure evidence incomplete | Failing test without `FAILURE_CAPTURE` record (§14.6) |
| 6 | ADG schema mapping changed mid-run | Schema freeze violated (§0 ADG SCHEMA FREEZE DISCIPLINE) |
| 7 | Repair began before clustering | Edit commit timestamp before cluster artifact timestamp |
| 8 | Test strictness weakened | Assertion removed, `assert True` added, mock broadened to hide failure |
| 9 | repair_class missing from commit | Commit touching production code without `repair_class:` footer |
| 10 | Policy drift misclassified | Governance module touched with `repair_class: production_bug_fix` without POLICY_DRIFT section |
| 11 | Contract conflict unresolved | Two conflicting contracts both touched without CONTRACT_CONFLICT section |
| 12 | Environment contract missing | subprocess/vLLM/CUDA failure without ENVIRONMENT_CONTRACT section |
| 13 | Repair run declared complete without full-suite evidence | Any claim of "repair complete" or "stabilization complete" without a post-repair full-suite green artifact (§7.3 condition 3–4) |

### 22.2 Integration with §5.1

The existing single entrypoint `python ops_scripts/ci/run_contract_gates.py` MUST enforce all 13 conditions in §22.1 in addition to its existing gates.

`ops_scripts/ci/check_ci_integrity.py` MUST be added to the gate sequence and run after the evidence contract checker.

